"``revoke cert`` takes a name that the local authority issues for on this "
"node, or a serial number in hexadecimal digits, as ``openssl x509 -noout "
"-serial`` prints it. The name gets a new certificate with a new key at "
"once, with no restart. The serial form also revokes a certificate that "
"this node no longer holds. A word that names nothing fails with "
"``ADM013``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../operations.rst:700
msgid ""
"The local authority keeps a revocation list in the directory ``local`` of "
"the storage: ``crl.pem``, and ``crl.der`` for a tool that reads DER. "
"Sibuna writes the list at the first internal name, also when nothing is "
"revoked, and writes it again after every revocation and at least every 12 "
"hours. A list is valid for 24 hours. A client does not find the list by "
