#: ../../operations.rst:2450
msgid ""
"We sign in, replace the temporary password, and open the page *Edge*. The "
"page shows four things."
msgstr ""

#: ../../operations.rst:2452
msgid ""
"**The node.** Its state is one of three words. *Serving* means that the "
"node admits new flows. *Draining* means that the node was told to stop: "
"it refuses new flows and finishes the open ones. *Full* means that the "
"flow table holds ``global.max_flows`` flows: the node refuses new flows "
"for lack of capacity. The table below the state gives the active flows "
"and the limit, the drops, the servers that are drained or down, the "
"reloads, the routing regime of the mesh and two revisions. The first "
"revision is the digest of the file, the one that ``show cluster`` prints. "
"The second is the revision of the database that the node serves in "
"persistent mode (SID 0028). A node that serves a file has none, and the "
"page says \"Not reported\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../operations.rst:2454
msgid ""
"**The refusals by cause.** One row for each reason of the metrics: "
"``flow_limit``, ``draining``, ``rate_limit``, ``connection_limit``, "
"``task_limit`` and the others. A node that refuses for lack of capacity "
"counts under ``flow_limit``, and a node that drains counts under "
"``draining``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../operations.rst:2456
msgid ""
"**The frontends and the pools.** A frontend shows its requests, flows, "
"bytes and the latency of a request: the mean and the 95th percentile. A "
"pool shows the columns of ``show servers`` for each server, then its "
"requests, failures, requests in flight and the wait for the first byte. A "
"view carries at most 256 servers, and the page says how many it left out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../operations.rst:2458
msgid ""
"**The fleet.** One row for each member: the state of the link, the state "
"of the node, its flows, its servers and its two revisions. A member whose "
"file differs from the file of this node is marked ``differs``. A member "
"that does not answer in five seconds has the row ``No answer``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../operations.rst:2460
msgid ""
"An operator or an administrator also sees the commands. Each command is "
"one line of the admin socket, and the function of the admin socket runs "
"it. The same parser checks it, the same worker applies it, and the same "
"limit of 20 commands in a burst and 10 per second holds. A change reaches "
"the other nodes over the mesh, as it does from ``sibuna ctl``, unless we "
"tick *This node only*."
msgstr ""

